{
  "_readme": "The lineup. Channel numbers are what you punch into the box. Each channel plays from named pools by daypart (days: 0=Sun..6=Sat, local time); gaps between dayparts are off-air (test pattern). Pools list YouTube sources: playlist/channel/video URLs or ytsearchN:query. Every source has a tier: legit (official uploader), wild (unofficial), filler (commercials, bumpers). Only tiers in `include` are built into the catalog. Rebuild with: python3 tools/build_catalog.py Commercials: shows start on the hour or half hour; the padding to the next boundary is commercials, spread as one or two act breaks inside the show (each up to breakSeconds, 150) with the rest after the credits; long broadcasts break about every 15 min. Block (music) channels break every breakEvery seconds between songs. breakEvery 0 on a channel = no commercials.",
